{
  "version": "2.1.0",
  "$schema": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/oasis-tcs/sarif-spec/main/sarif-2.1/schema/sarif-schema-2.1.0.json",
  "runs": [
    {
      "tool": {
        "driver": {
          "fullName": "Trivy Vulnerability Scanner",
          "informationUri": "https://github.com/aquasecurity/trivy",
          "name": "Trivy",
          "rules": [
            {
              "id": "CVE-2026-68770",
              "name": "LanguageSpecificPackageVulnerability",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "sentence-transformers: sentence-transformers: Remote Code Execution via Security Control Bypass"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "sentence-transformers contains a security control bypass vulnerability that allows attackers to achieve arbitrary code execution by exploiting a logic flaw in the import_module_class helper within sentence_transformers/util/misc.py, where the guard condition includes an 'or os.path.exists(model_name_or_path)' clause that satisfies the trust gate whenever the supplied path exists on the local filesystem, regardless of the trust_remote_code=False argument. Attackers who can control or influence the contents of a model directory on disk can place malicious Python files such as modeling_*.py referenced via modules.json, causing the code to execute at import time when an application loads the model with SentenceTransformer(path, trust_remote_code=False), bypassing the documented security contract and achieving code execution within the loading process."
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "error"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-68770",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2026-68770\nSeverity: CRITICAL\nPackage: sentence-transformers\nFixed Version: 5.6.0\nLink: [CVE-2026-68770](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-68770)\nsentence-transformers contains a security control bypass vulnerability that allows attackers to achieve arbitrary code execution by exploiting a logic flaw in the import_module_class helper within sentence_transformers/util/misc.py, where the guard condition includes an 'or os.path.exists(model_name_or_path)' clause that satisfies the trust gate whenever the supplied path exists on the local filesystem, regardless of the trust_remote_code=False argument. Attackers who can control or influence the contents of a model directory on disk can place malicious Python files such as modeling_*.py referenced via modules.json, causing the code to execute at import time when an application loads the model with SentenceTransformer(path, trust_remote_code=False), bypassing the documented security contract and achieving code execution within the loading process.",
                "markdown": "**Vulnerability CVE-2026-68770**\n| Severity | Package | Fixed Version | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|CRITICAL|sentence-transformers|5.6.0|[CVE-2026-68770](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-68770)|\n\nsentence-transformers contains a security control bypass vulnerability that allows attackers to achieve arbitrary code execution by exploiting a logic flaw in the import_module_class helper within sentence_transformers/util/misc.py, where the guard condition includes an 'or os.path.exists(model_name_or_path)' clause that satisfies the trust gate whenever the supplied path exists on the local filesystem, regardless of the trust_remote_code=False argument. Attackers who can control or influence the contents of a model directory on disk can place malicious Python files such as modeling_*.py referenced via modules.json, causing the code to execute at import time when an application loads the model with SentenceTransformer(path, trust_remote_code=False), bypassing the documented security contract and achieving code execution within the loading process."
              },
              "properties": {
                "cvssv3_baseScore": 9.8,
                "cvssv3_vector": "CVSS:3.1/AV:N/AC:L/PR:N/UI:N/S:U/C:H/I:H/A:H",
                "cvssv40_baseScore": 9.3,
                "cvssv40_vector": "CVSS:4.0/AV:N/AC:L/AT:N/PR:N/UI:N/VC:H/VI:H/VA:H/SC:N/SI:N/SA:N",
                "precision": "very-high",
                "security-severity": "9.8",
                "tags": [
                  "vulnerability",
                  "security",
                  "CRITICAL"
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "CVE-2026-90711",
              "name": "LanguageSpecificPackageVulnerability",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "proxy-addr: proxy-addr vulnerable to IP spoofing via IPv4-mapped IPv6 trust subnet"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "proxy-addr is a Node.js module that determines a request's client address behind trusted reverse proxies, and it backs Express req.ip and req.ips. In versions 1.1.0 through 2.0.7, a trust subnet written in IPv4-mapped IPv6 notation with an IPv4-sized prefix, such as ::ffff:10.0.0.0/8 instead of the correct ::ffff:10.0.0.0/104, is accepted without error but trusts every IPv4 address on the internet rather than the block it names. Because the socket peer then becomes trusted at hop 0, any unauthenticated client can supply an arbitrary X-Forwarded-For header and control the address the application reads, which defeats IP-based access control, rate limiting, geolocation, and audit logging. This is a fail-open regression introduced in version 1.1.0. The issue is fixed in proxy-addr 2.0.8, and users should upgrade to 2.0.8 or later. As a workaround, ensure any IPv4-mapped IPv6 trust subnet uses a prefix length of at least 97, or express the range in plain IPv4 notation."
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "error"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-90711",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2026-90711\nSeverity: CRITICAL\nPackage: proxy-addr\nFixed Version: 2.0.8\nLink: [CVE-2026-90711](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-90711)\nproxy-addr is a Node.js module that determines a request's client address behind trusted reverse proxies, and it backs Express req.ip and req.ips. In versions 1.1.0 through 2.0.7, a trust subnet written in IPv4-mapped IPv6 notation with an IPv4-sized prefix, such as ::ffff:10.0.0.0/8 instead of the correct ::ffff:10.0.0.0/104, is accepted without error but trusts every IPv4 address on the internet rather than the block it names. Because the socket peer then becomes trusted at hop 0, any unauthenticated client can supply an arbitrary X-Forwarded-For header and control the address the application reads, which defeats IP-based access control, rate limiting, geolocation, and audit logging. This is a fail-open regression introduced in version 1.1.0. The issue is fixed in proxy-addr 2.0.8, and users should upgrade to 2.0.8 or later. As a workaround, ensure any IPv4-mapped IPv6 trust subnet uses a prefix length of at least 97, or express the range in plain IPv4 notation.",
                "markdown": "**Vulnerability CVE-2026-90711**\n| Severity | Package | Fixed Version | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|CRITICAL|proxy-addr|2.0.8|[CVE-2026-90711](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-90711)|\n\nproxy-addr is a Node.js module that determines a request's client address behind trusted reverse proxies, and it backs Express req.ip and req.ips. In versions 1.1.0 through 2.0.7, a trust subnet written in IPv4-mapped IPv6 notation with an IPv4-sized prefix, such as ::ffff:10.0.0.0/8 instead of the correct ::ffff:10.0.0.0/104, is accepted without error but trusts every IPv4 address on the internet rather than the block it names. Because the socket peer then becomes trusted at hop 0, any unauthenticated client can supply an arbitrary X-Forwarded-For header and control the address the application reads, which defeats IP-based access control, rate limiting, geolocation, and audit logging. This is a fail-open regression introduced in version 1.1.0. The issue is fixed in proxy-addr 2.0.8, and users should upgrade to 2.0.8 or later. As a workaround, ensure any IPv4-mapped IPv6 trust subnet uses a prefix length of at least 97, or express the range in plain IPv4 notation."
              },
              "properties": {
                "cvssv3_baseScore": 9.1,
                "cvssv3_vector": "CVSS:3.1/AV:N/AC:L/PR:N/UI:N/S:U/C:H/I:H/A:N",
                "precision": "very-high",
                "security-severity": "9.1",
                "tags": [
                  "vulnerability",
                  "security",
                  "CRITICAL"
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "CVE-2026-63374",
              "name": "LanguageSpecificPackageVulnerability",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "anyio: AnyIO: TLS certificate spoofing via improper internationalized domain name encoding"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "AnyIO is a high level asynchronous concurrency and networking framework that works on top of either Trio or asyncio. Prior to 4.14.2, connect_tcp() and TLSStream.wrap() can validate internationalized host names after the standard library converts them with IDNA 2003 instead of IDNA 2008. When a connection to a non-ASCII domain is hijacked or redirected, an attacker can obtain a legitimate certificate for the different ASCII hostname produced by IDNA 2003 and present it to the client, causing the malicious endpoint's certificate to validate. This issue is fixed in version 4.14.2."
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "error"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-63374",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2026-63374\nSeverity: CRITICAL\nPackage: anyio\nFixed Version: 4.14.2\nLink: [CVE-2026-63374](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-63374)\nAnyIO is a high level asynchronous concurrency and networking framework that works on top of either Trio or asyncio. Prior to 4.14.2, connect_tcp() and TLSStream.wrap() can validate internationalized host names after the standard library converts them with IDNA 2003 instead of IDNA 2008. When a connection to a non-ASCII domain is hijacked or redirected, an attacker can obtain a legitimate certificate for the different ASCII hostname produced by IDNA 2003 and present it to the client, causing the malicious endpoint's certificate to validate. This issue is fixed in version 4.14.2.",
                "markdown": "**Vulnerability CVE-2026-63374**\n| Severity | Package | Fixed Version | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|CRITICAL|anyio|4.14.2|[CVE-2026-63374](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-63374)|\n\nAnyIO is a high level asynchronous concurrency and networking framework that works on top of either Trio or asyncio. Prior to 4.14.2, connect_tcp() and TLSStream.wrap() can validate internationalized host names after the standard library converts them with IDNA 2003 instead of IDNA 2008. When a connection to a non-ASCII domain is hijacked or redirected, an attacker can obtain a legitimate certificate for the different ASCII hostname produced by IDNA 2003 and present it to the client, causing the malicious endpoint's certificate to validate. This issue is fixed in version 4.14.2."
              },
              "properties": {
                "cvssv40_baseScore": 9.3,
                "cvssv40_vector": "CVSS:4.0/AV:N/AC:L/AT:N/PR:N/UI:N/VC:H/VI:H/VA:N/SC:N/SI:N/SA:N",
                "precision": "very-high",
                "security-severity": "9.5",
                "tags": [
                  "vulnerability",
                  "security",
                  "CRITICAL"
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "CVE-2026-114139",
              "name": "LanguageSpecificPackageVulnerability",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "Sentry-Javascript: Middleware Bypass when using Tunnel route"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "Sentry-Javascript is an official Sentry SDKs for JavaScript. From 9.36.0 until 9.47.2, 10.75.2, and 11.0.0-rc.1, the webpack integration for @sentry/nextjs skips application middleware for every request path under a configured tunnelRoute, while the tunnel rewrite serves only the exact tunnel path with valid o and p query parameters. When an application route directly collides with the tunnel path or a root dynamic segment resolves under it, an unauthenticated request can reach that route without middleware authorization. Exploitation requires tunnelRoute, a webpack build, a colliding route, and middleware being the only authorization control. This issue is fixed in versions 9.47.2, 10.75.2, and 11.0.0-rc.1."
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "error"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-114139",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2026-114139\nSeverity: CRITICAL\nPackage: @sentry/nextjs\nFixed Version: 9.47.2, 10.75.2, 11.0.0-rc.1\nLink: [CVE-2026-114139](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-114139)\nSentry-Javascript is an official Sentry SDKs for JavaScript. From 9.36.0 until 9.47.2, 10.75.2, and 11.0.0-rc.1, the webpack integration for @sentry/nextjs skips application middleware for every request path under a configured tunnelRoute, while the tunnel rewrite serves only the exact tunnel path with valid o and p query parameters. When an application route directly collides with the tunnel path or a root dynamic segment resolves under it, an unauthenticated request can reach that route without middleware authorization. Exploitation requires tunnelRoute, a webpack build, a colliding route, and middleware being the only authorization control. This issue is fixed in versions 9.47.2, 10.75.2, and 11.0.0-rc.1.",
                "markdown": "**Vulnerability CVE-2026-114139**\n| Severity | Package | Fixed Version | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|CRITICAL|@sentry/nextjs|9.47.2, 10.75.2, 11.0.0-rc.1|[CVE-2026-114139](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-114139)|\n\nSentry-Javascript is an official Sentry SDKs for JavaScript. From 9.36.0 until 9.47.2, 10.75.2, and 11.0.0-rc.1, the webpack integration for @sentry/nextjs skips application middleware for every request path under a configured tunnelRoute, while the tunnel rewrite serves only the exact tunnel path with valid o and p query parameters. When an application route directly collides with the tunnel path or a root dynamic segment resolves under it, an unauthenticated request can reach that route without middleware authorization. Exploitation requires tunnelRoute, a webpack build, a colliding route, and middleware being the only authorization control. This issue is fixed in versions 9.47.2, 10.75.2, and 11.0.0-rc.1."
              },
              "properties": {
                "cvssv40_baseScore": 9.1,
                "cvssv40_vector": "CVSS:4.0/AV:N/AC:L/AT:P/PR:N/UI:N/VC:H/VI:H/VA:N/SC:N/SI:N/SA:N",
                "precision": "very-high",
                "security-severity": "9.5",
                "tags": [
                  "vulnerability",
                  "security",
                  "CRITICAL"
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "CVE-2026-85061",
              "name": "LanguageSpecificPackageVulnerability",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "MapLibre GL JS: XSS Sanitizer Bypass in DOM.sanitize() via Live NamedNodeMap Removal Skip"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "MapLibre GL JS is an interactive vector tile map library for web browsers. Prior to 6.4.1, DOM.sanitize() in src/util/dom.ts iterates elem.attributes as a live NamedNodeMap while removeAttributes() removes attributes from the same collection, shifting indexes and skipping an adjacent dangerous attribute. An attacker who controls untrusted third-party style attribution strings or user-supplied custom attributions can supply consecutive dangerous attributes, causing an attribute such as onload or ontoggle to survive sanitization and execute when the attribution control inserts the content into innerHTML. A victim must render the affected map content for the script to execute. This issue is fixed in version 6.4.1."
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "error"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-85061",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2026-85061\nSeverity: CRITICAL\nPackage: maplibre-gl\nFixed Version: 6.4.1\nLink: [CVE-2026-85061](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-85061)\nMapLibre GL JS is an interactive vector tile map library for web browsers. Prior to 6.4.1, DOM.sanitize() in src/util/dom.ts iterates elem.attributes as a live NamedNodeMap while removeAttributes() removes attributes from the same collection, shifting indexes and skipping an adjacent dangerous attribute. An attacker who controls untrusted third-party style attribution strings or user-supplied custom attributions can supply consecutive dangerous attributes, causing an attribute such as onload or ontoggle to survive sanitization and execute when the attribution control inserts the content into innerHTML. A victim must render the affected map content for the script to execute. This issue is fixed in version 6.4.1.",
                "markdown": "**Vulnerability CVE-2026-85061**\n| Severity | Package | Fixed Version | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|CRITICAL|maplibre-gl|6.4.1|[CVE-2026-85061](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-85061)|\n\nMapLibre GL JS is an interactive vector tile map library for web browsers. Prior to 6.4.1, DOM.sanitize() in src/util/dom.ts iterates elem.attributes as a live NamedNodeMap while removeAttributes() removes attributes from the same collection, shifting indexes and skipping an adjacent dangerous attribute. An attacker who controls untrusted third-party style attribution strings or user-supplied custom attributions can supply consecutive dangerous attributes, causing an attribute such as onload or ontoggle to survive sanitization and execute when the attribution control inserts the content into innerHTML. A victim must render the affected map content for the script to execute. This issue is fixed in version 6.4.1."
              },
              "properties": {
                "cvssv3_baseScore": 10,
                "cvssv3_vector": "CVSS:3.1/AV:N/AC:L/PR:N/UI:N/S:C/C:H/I:H/A:N",
                "precision": "very-high",
                "security-severity": "10.0",
                "tags": [
                  "vulnerability",
                  "security",
                  "CRITICAL"
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "CVE-2026-75604",
              "name": "LanguageSpecificPackageVulnerability",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "next: Next.js: Unauthenticated Remote Code Execution on windows-hosted servers"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "Next.js is a React framework for building full-stack web applications. From 13.4.0 until 15.5.24 and 16.3.3, Next.js applications using Pages Router or App Router without Cache Components on Windows-hosted servers do not consistently escape backslashes in route segments before constructing incremental-cache paths. In packages/next/src/shared/lib/router/utils/escape-path-delimiters.ts and packages/next/src/server/lib/incremental-cache/file-system-cache.ts, a remote request can supply encoded Windows path separators that traverse outside the intended cache root and expose private build data, including the server-reference-manifest encryption key. Disclosure of that key can enable remote code execution in the affected application. This issue is fixed in versions 15.5.24 and 16.3.3."
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "error"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-75604",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2026-75604\nSeverity: CRITICAL\nPackage: next\nFixed Version: 15.5.24, 16.3.3\nLink: [CVE-2026-75604](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-75604)\nNext.js is a React framework for building full-stack web applications. From 13.4.0 until 15.5.24 and 16.3.3, Next.js applications using Pages Router or App Router without Cache Components on Windows-hosted servers do not consistently escape backslashes in route segments before constructing incremental-cache paths. In packages/next/src/shared/lib/router/utils/escape-path-delimiters.ts and packages/next/src/server/lib/incremental-cache/file-system-cache.ts, a remote request can supply encoded Windows path separators that traverse outside the intended cache root and expose private build data, including the server-reference-manifest encryption key. Disclosure of that key can enable remote code execution in the affected application. This issue is fixed in versions 15.5.24 and 16.3.3.",
                "markdown": "**Vulnerability CVE-2026-75604**\n| Severity | Package | Fixed Version | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|CRITICAL|next|15.5.24, 16.3.3|[CVE-2026-75604](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-75604)|\n\nNext.js is a React framework for building full-stack web applications. From 13.4.0 until 15.5.24 and 16.3.3, Next.js applications using Pages Router or App Router without Cache Components on Windows-hosted servers do not consistently escape backslashes in route segments before constructing incremental-cache paths. In packages/next/src/shared/lib/router/utils/escape-path-delimiters.ts and packages/next/src/server/lib/incremental-cache/file-system-cache.ts, a remote request can supply encoded Windows path separators that traverse outside the intended cache root and expose private build data, including the server-reference-manifest encryption key. Disclosure of that key can enable remote code execution in the affected application. This issue is fixed in versions 15.5.24 and 16.3.3."
              },
              "properties": {
                "cvssv3_baseScore": 9.1,
                "cvssv3_vector": "CVSS:3.1/AV:N/AC:H/PR:N/UI:N/S:C/C:H/I:H/A:H",
                "precision": "very-high",
                "security-severity": "9.1",
                "tags": [
                  "vulnerability",
                  "security",
                  "CRITICAL"
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "GHSA-2464-fhr4-w9xw",
              "name": "LanguageSpecificPackageVulnerability",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "Next.js: Unauthenticated Remote Code Execution in Image Optimization API when SVG files are used"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "## Impact\n\nA memory-related vulnerability has been discovered in an upstream library used for Image Optimization can lead to possible remote code execution (RCE) when Next.js runs on glibc-based Linux.\n\n## Workaround\n\nEnsure the version of `sharp` used by Next.js is greater than or equal to `0.35.5`. Fresh installs automatically get a fixed version of `sharp`.\nUpgrading Next.js to the patched versions will ensure package managers automatically provide a fixed version of `sharp` to Next.js."
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "error"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://github.com/advisories/GHSA-2464-fhr4-w9xw",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability GHSA-2464-fhr4-w9xw\nSeverity: CRITICAL\nPackage: next\nFixed Version: 15.5.28, 16.4.1\nLink: [GHSA-2464-fhr4-w9xw](https://github.com/advisories/GHSA-2464-fhr4-w9xw)\n## Impact\n\nA memory-related vulnerability has been discovered in an upstream library used for Image Optimization can lead to possible remote code execution (RCE) when Next.js runs on glibc-based Linux.\n\n## Workaround\n\nEnsure the version of `sharp` used by Next.js is greater than or equal to `0.35.5`. Fresh installs automatically get a fixed version of `sharp`.\nUpgrading Next.js to the patched versions will ensure package managers automatically provide a fixed version of `sharp` to Next.js.",
                "markdown": "**Vulnerability GHSA-2464-fhr4-w9xw**\n| Severity | Package | Fixed Version | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|CRITICAL|next|15.5.28, 16.4.1|[GHSA-2464-fhr4-w9xw](https://github.com/advisories/GHSA-2464-fhr4-w9xw)|\n\n## Impact\n\nA memory-related vulnerability has been discovered in an upstream library used for Image Optimization can lead to possible remote code execution (RCE) when Next.js runs on glibc-based Linux.\n\n## Workaround\n\nEnsure the version of `sharp` used by Next.js is greater than or equal to `0.35.5`. Fresh installs automatically get a fixed version of `sharp`.\nUpgrading Next.js to the patched versions will ensure package managers automatically provide a fixed version of `sharp` to Next.js."
              },
              "properties": {
                "cvssv40_baseScore": 9.5,
                "cvssv40_vector": "CVSS:4.0/AV:N/AC:L/AT:P/PR:N/UI:N/VC:H/VI:H/VA:H/SC:H/SI:H/SA:H",
                "precision": "very-high",
                "security-severity": "9.5",
                "tags": [
                  "vulnerability",
                  "security",
                  "CRITICAL"
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "GHSA-2xp9-vwfh-vxw4",
              "name": "LanguageSpecificPackageVulnerability",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "Next.js: Unauthenticated Remote Code Execution in Image Optimization API when AVIF files are used"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "A vulnerability in the underlying `libheif` library used by `sharp` which Next.js uses for image optimization can lead to remote code execution when AVIF files are optimized.\n\nUntil a fix has propagated, optimization of AVIF files is disabled."
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "error"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://github.com/advisories/GHSA-2xp9-vwfh-vxw4",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability GHSA-2xp9-vwfh-vxw4\nSeverity: CRITICAL\nPackage: next\nFixed Version: 15.5.24, 16.3.3\nLink: [GHSA-2xp9-vwfh-vxw4](https://github.com/advisories/GHSA-2xp9-vwfh-vxw4)\nA vulnerability in the underlying `libheif` library used by `sharp` which Next.js uses for image optimization can lead to remote code execution when AVIF files are optimized.\n\nUntil a fix has propagated, optimization of AVIF files is disabled.",
                "markdown": "**Vulnerability GHSA-2xp9-vwfh-vxw4**\n| Severity | Package | Fixed Version | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|CRITICAL|next|15.5.24, 16.3.3|[GHSA-2xp9-vwfh-vxw4](https://github.com/advisories/GHSA-2xp9-vwfh-vxw4)|\n\nA vulnerability in the underlying `libheif` library used by `sharp` which Next.js uses for image optimization can lead to remote code execution when AVIF files are optimized.\n\nUntil a fix has propagated, optimization of AVIF files is disabled."
              },
              "properties": {
                "cvssv40_baseScore": 9.5,
                "cvssv40_vector": "CVSS:4.0/AV:N/AC:L/AT:P/PR:N/UI:N/VC:H/VI:H/VA:H/SC:H/SI:H/SA:H",
